          "jcr:created": "Wed Sep 11 2019 19:43:16 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><b>Description:&nbsp;<br>\n </b>Joint infection is one of the most common reasons for concern in Shoulder Arthroplasty. Join us as Dr. Willis presents the latest research in infections around diagnosing, preventing and treating infection shoulder arthroplasty.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><b>Learning objective:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Specifics of Cutibacterium acnes (Propionibacterium acnes) &amp; the shoulder biome</li>\n<li>Diagnosis &amp; Management of infections in shoulder arthroplasty</li>\n<li>Steps to reduce bacterial burden of infections<ul>\n<li>Preoperatively</li>\n<li>Intraoperatively</li>\n<li>Postoperatively<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Course instructor:</b> Matthew Willis, MD</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Feb 26 2020 15:28:25 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
